### Peticiones de prueba para booking-service (Sesión 4)
### IntelliJ IDEA (HTTP Client): los login guardan el token con client.global.set(...).
### VS Code (REST Client): copia el accessToken de cada login en la variable {{...Token}} correspondiente.
### Requiere user-service (8084), event-service (8081) y payment-service (8083) en marcha. Ejecuta primero los login; Postman guarda los tokens y los ids de las reservas creadas.

@host = http://localhost:8082/api/v1
@auth = http://localhost:8084/api/v1
@actuator = http://localhost:8082/actuator
# Cambia estos valores por los ids que devuelven las peticiones "Crear ..."
@bookingId = 1
@bigBookingId = 2

### ---------- AUTENTICACIÓN (ejecutar primero) ----------

### Login CUSTOMER Ana (ana@mail.com) -> 200
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@mail.com",
  "password": "Customer123!"
}

> {% client.global.set("anaToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Login CUSTOMER Luis (luis@mail.com) -> 200
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "luis@mail.com",
  "password": "Customer123!"
}

> {% client.global.set("luisToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Login ORGANIZER (organizer@ticketing.pe) -> 200
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "organizer@ticketing.pe",
  "password": "Organizer123!"
}

> {% client.global.set("organizerToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### Login ADMIN (admin@ticketing.pe) -> 200
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@ticketing.pe",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### ---------- RESERVAS ----------

### Crear reserva como Ana -> 201 (el cliente sale del token)
POST {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "ticketCategoryId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

### S4: Crear reserva sin token -> 401
POST {{host}}/bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "ticketCategoryId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

### S4: Crear reserva como ORGANIZER -> 403 (solo CUSTOMER compra)
POST {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{organizerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "ticketCategoryId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

### Crear reserva inválida -> 400 con lista de errores
POST {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ticketCategoryId": 1,
  "quantity": 15
}

### Zona que no pertenece al evento -> 400 (event-service respondió 404)
POST {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "ticketCategoryId": 4,
  "quantity": 1
}

### Obtener mi reserva -> 200
GET {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}

### S4: Obtener la reserva de Ana como Luis -> 403 (no es el dueño)
GET {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{luisToken}}

### S4: Obtener la reserva de Ana como ADMIN -> 200
GET {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Listar mis reservas -> 200
GET {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}

### S4: Luis filtra por el correo de Ana -> solo ve las suyas -> 200
GET {{host}}/bookings?customerEmail=ana@mail.com
Authorization: Bearer {{luisToken}}

### ADMIN lista las reservas de Ana -> 200
GET {{host}}/bookings?customerEmail=ana@mail.com
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Reserva inexistente -> 404
GET {{host}}/bookings/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}

### ---------- PAGOS ----------

### S4: Luis intenta pagar la reserva de Ana -> 403
POST {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{luisToken}}

### Pagar reserva -> 200 (booking-service reenvía el token de Ana a payment-service)
POST {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}

### Tickets emitidos -> 200
GET {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}

### Pagar otra vez -> 409
POST {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}

### Cancelar una reserva confirmada -> 409
PATCH {{host}}/bookings/{{bookingId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{anaToken}}

### Luis reserva 10 entradas VIP (S/ 4500) -> 201
POST {{host}}/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{luisToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": 1,
  "ticketCategoryId": 1,
  "quantity": 10
}

### Pagar la reserva de S/ 4500 -> 402 (supera el límite de la tarjeta)
POST {{host}}/bookings/{{bigBookingId}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{luisToken}}

### La reserva rechazada sigue PENDING -> 200
GET {{host}}/bookings/{{bigBookingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{luisToken}}

### ---------- RESILIENCIA (Actuator, público en desarrollo) ----------

### Estado de los Circuit Breakers -> 200
GET {{actuator}}/circuitbreakers

### Health (incluye el estado de los circuitos) -> 200
GET {{actuator}}/health
